Reject both linkage features at compile time

Cargo features are additive, so nothing stops a caller asking for `full`
and `full-dynamic` together — and the result would be `dynamic-linking`
silently winning over the vendored build, or not, depending on
rdkafka-sys' internals. Fail with an explanation instead.

This is also why CI cannot use `--all-features`; upstream's `lint-all`
feature exists for that.
